> 		polymorph control by the time they are eating this wand.
> 		Ideas? )
> 	secret door detection
> 	create monster ( should this make you satiated? )

Sure... creates a monster in your stomach.  Maybe you could figure out
which monster would be created and add the appropriate amount to your
hunger status as if you had eaten the corpse.  If you want to get
really silly, you could include the chance of gaining intrinsics
and/or negative effects (rotten meat from undead corpses, poison from
poisonous corpses, instadeath from foo-trice corpses!)

> 	nothing ( perhaps this should have no effect? )

Wand does nothing, I don't think eating it should do anything either. 
In fact, I think it should be removed from the game altogether.

> 	opening ( should this make you hungry, like /oDigging? )

It's the opposite of locking (based on wand effects)... why not a
similar chance to lose disintegration resistance?

> 	probing

Self probing... about as useful as eating a wand of enlightenment vs.
zapping the wand.

> 	wishing

Instadeath... you'll *wish* you hadn't done that! :->
 	
> I'm also thinking that most wands should have a chance to gain energy,
> similar to a !oEnergy -- perhaps, say, from 1 to 2 * charges (4 *
> charges if blessed).

That's actually much more than a !oGE gives you.  You get 5 + d5 for
an uncursed potion, twice that for a blessed potion.  Non-directional
wands can have as much as 15 charges... I don't think you should have
a chance of getting 60 Pw from a blessed wand of secret door detection
(0:15).

If you want to go this route, make the chance exclusive from other
effects and make it no more than rnd(obj->spe).  This way, you would
have a 1 in 15 chance of getting 15 Pw from a fully-charged,
non-directional wand iff you got no other effects.
 
